T ... {user} ...\\\\\"` dynamically alters SQL syntax.\\\\n3. Attacker can bypass auth with `' OR '1'='1' --`.\\\\n\\\\n#### Secure Remediation:\\\\n```python\\\\n@app.route('/login', methods=['POST'])\\\\ndef login():\\\\n    user = request.form.get('user', '')\\\\n    pwd = request.form.get('pwd', '')\\\\n    query = \\\\\"SELECT * FROM accounts WHERE user = ? AND pass = ?\\\\\"\\\\n    return db.execute(query, (user, pwd)).fetchall()\\\\n```\"}\n        ]\n    },\n    # CWE-78: Command Injection\n    {\n        \"messages\": [\n            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Review this Node.js script:\\\\n\\\\nconst { exec } = require('child_process');\\\\napp.get('/backup', (req, res) => {\\\\n    const folder = req.query.folder;\\\\n    exec(`zip -r backup.zip ${folder}`, (err) => res.send('Done'));\\\\n});\"},\n            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"### Security Assessment by Fluxnat Coder 3B\\\\n\\\\n**Severity:** Critical (CVSS 9.8)\\\\n**Vulnerability:** Command Injection\\\\n**CWE:** CWE-78\\\\n**OWASP:** A03:2021 - Injection\\\\n\\\\n#### Root Cause & Reasoning:\\\\n1. `req.query.folder` is passed unescaped to `child_process.exec`.\\\\n2. The system shell evaluates metacharacters (`;`, `|`, `&`).\\\\n3. Payload `folder=data; rm -rf /` executes arbitrary OS commands.\\\\n\\\\n#### Secure Remediation:\\\\n```javascript\\\\nconst { execFile } = require('child_process');\\\\nconst path = require('path');\\\\n\\\\napp.get('/backup', (req, res) => {\\\\n    const folder = path.basename(req.query.folder || '');\\\\n    if (!folder || !/^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$/.test(folder)) {\\\\n        return res.status(400).send('Invalid folder parameter');\\\\n    }\\\\n    execFile('zip', ['-r', 'backup.zip', folder], (err) => {\\\\n        if (err) return res.status(500).send('Error');\\\\n        res.send('Backup created');\\\\n    });\\\\n});\\\\n```\"}\n        ]\n    },\n    # CWE-22: Path Traversal\n    {\n        \"messages\": [\n            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Check this path handling:\\\\n\\\\n@app.route('/read')\\\\ndef read_doc():\\\\n    doc = request.args.get('doc')\\\\n    return open('/srv/docs/' + doc).read()\"},\n            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"### Security Assessment by Fluxnat Coder 3B\\\\n\\\\n**Severity:** High (CVSS 7.5)\\\\n**Vulnerability:** Path Traversal / Arbitrary File Read\\\\n**CWE:** CWE-22\\\\n**OWASP:** A01:2021 - Broken Access Control\\\\n\\\\n#### Root Cause & Reasoning:\\\\n1. Input parameter `doc` accepts traversal sequences like `../../../../etc/passwd`.\\\\n2. Direct string concatenation fails to confine the path to the intended directory.\\\\n\\\\n#### Secure Remediation:\\\\n```python\\\\nimport os\\\\nfrom werkzeug.utils import secure_filename\\\\n\\\\nBASE_DIR = os.path.realpath('/srv/docs')\\\\n\\\\n@app.route('/read')\\\\ndef read_doc():\\\\n    doc = secure_filename(request.args.get('doc', ''))\\\\n    target = os.path.realpath(os.path.join(BASE_DIR, doc))\\\\n    if not target.startswith(BASE_DIR + os.sep) or not os.path.isfile(target):\\\\n        return 'Access Denied', 403\\\\n    with open(target, 'r') as f:\\\\n        return f.read()\\\\n```\"}\n        ]\n    },\n    # CWE-79: Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)\n    {\n        \"messages\": [\n            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Audit this PHP code for web security vulnerabilities:\\\\n\\\\n<?php\\\\n$search = $_GET['q'];\\\\necho \\\\\"<h1>Search results for: \\\\\" . $search . \\\\\"</h1>\\\\\";\\\\n?>\"},\n            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"### Security Assessment by Fluxnat Coder 3B\\\\n\\\\n**Severity:** High (CVSS 7.1)\\\\n**Vulnerability:** Reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)\\\\n**CWE:** CWE-79\\\\n**OWASP:** A03:2021 - Injection\\\\n\\\\n#### Root Cause & Reasoning:\\\\n1. `$_GET['q']` takes untrusted client input directly.\\\\n2. Output is echoed directly into HTML response body without escaping.\\\\n3. Malicious `<script>` tags execute in victim's browser context.\\\\n\\\\n#### Secure Remediation:\\\\n```php\\\\n<?php\\\\n$search = isset($_GET['q']) ? $_GET['q'] : '';\\\\necho \\\\\"<h1>Search results for: \\\\\" . htmlspecialchars($search, ENT_QUOTES | ENT_SUBSTITUTE, 'UTF-8') . \\\\\"</h1>\\\\\";\\\\n?>\\\\n```\"}\n        ]\n    },\n    # CWE-502: Insecure Deserialization\n    {\n        \"messages\": [\n            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Audit this session restoration handler:\\\\n\\\\nimport pickle, base64\\\\n@app.route('/state')\\\\ndef restore():\\\\n    raw = base64.b64decode(request.cookies['session'])\\\\n    return pickle.loads(raw).name\"},\n            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"### Security Assessment by Fluxnat Coder 3B\\\\n\\\\n**Severity:** Critical (CVSS 9.8)\\\\n**Vulnerability:** Insecure Deserialization\\\\n**CWE:** CWE-502\\\\n**OWASP:** A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures\\\\n\\\\n#### Root Cause & Reasoning:\\\\n1. Untrusted cookie data is parsed directly with Python `pickle`.\\\\n2. `pickle` allows arbitrary callable execution via `__reduce__`.\\\\n3. Attackers gain Remote Code Execution (RCE).\\\\n\\\\n#### Secure Remediation:\\\\nUse safe JSON serialization or cryptographically signed session tokens instead of pickle.\"}\n        ]\n    },\n    # CWE-918: Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)\n    {\n        \"messages\": [\n            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"What security risk exists in this Go HTTP handler?\\\\n\\\\nfunc preview(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\\\\n    url := r.URL.Query().Get(\\\\\"url\\\\\")\\\\n    resp, _ := http.Get(url)\\\\n    io.Copy(w, resp.Body)\\\\n}\"},\n            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"### Security Assessment by Fluxnat Coder 3B\\\\n\\\\n**Severity:** High (CVSS 8.6)\\\\n**Vulnerability:** Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)\\\\n**CWE:** CWE-918\\\\n**OWASP:** A10:2021 - Server-Side Request Forgery\\\\n\\\\n#### Root Cause & Reasoning:\\\\n1. Untrusted `url` parameter is passed directly to `http.Get`.\\\\n2. Outgoing requests originate from inside the internal network perimeter.\\\\n3. Attackers can access internal metadata APIs (169.254.169.254) and local microservices.\\\\n\\\\n#### Secure Remediation:\\\\nValidate scheme to HTTPS, resolve hostname to IP, block private/loopback ranges (RFC 1918), and enforce domain allowlists.\"}\n        ]\n    },\n    # CWE-798: Hardcoded Secrets\n    {\n        \"messages\": [\n            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Inspect this client config:\\\\n\\\\nAWS_KEY = \\\\\"AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE\\\\\"\\\\nAWS_SEC = \\\\\"wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY\\\\\"\\\\nclient = boto3.client('s3', aws_access_key_id=AWS_KEY, aws_secret_access_key=AWS_SEC)\"},\n            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"### Security Assessment by Fluxnat Coder 3B\\\\n\\\\n**Severity:** High (CVSS 7.5)\\\\n**Vulnerability:** Hardcoded Credentials\\\\n**CWE:** CWE-798\\\\n**OWASP:** A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures\\\\n\\\\n#### Root Cause & Reasoning:\\\\n1. Plaintext AWS credentials are hardcoded directly into source code.\\\\n2. Committing code to version control leaks long-lived secrets.\\\\n\\\\n#### Secure Remediation:\\\\nLoad credentials from environment variables or IAM instance profile roles: `client = boto3.client('s3')`.\"}\n        ]\n    },\n    # CWE-120: Buffer Overflow\n    {\n        \"messages\": [\n            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Review this C code:\\\\n\\\\nvoid copy_data(char *input) {\\\\n    char buf[64];