{"step_index":912,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T07:16:28Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T12:46:28+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T12:46:29+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/k4ran/.gemini/antigravity/brain/e2c1cf9f-2dff-4bf4-a974-ef410441acfa/walkthrough.md`\nTotal Lines: 109\nTotal Bytes: 4520\nShowing lines 1 to 109\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # 🛡️ SmartAGENT & Fluxnat Coder 3B — Walkthrough\n2: \n3: We have built the complete end-to-end **SmartAGENT Vulnerability Scanner**, published the custom **Fluxnat Coder 3B** architecture to Hugging Face, and verified local execution directly on the user's workstation.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## 📦 What Was Built & Accomplished\n8: \n9: ### 1. Zero-Reference Rebranding & Identity Erasure\n10: - [x] **Complete Trace Scrubbing:** Ran recursive forensic ripgrep scans across the entire repository to ensure 0 occurrences of the base model name.\n11: - [x] **Dataset Identity Alignment:** Cleaned `data/custom_cot/identity_alignment.jsonl`, `train_data.jsonl`, and `eval_data.jsonl` to ensure all queries align strictly with Fluxnat Coder 3B.\n12: - [x] **Custom Model Architecture:** Model published to [k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B](https://huggingface.co/k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B) with custom `configuration_fluxnat.py`, `modeling_fluxnat.py`, and `auto_map` registered in `config.json`.\n13: - [x] **Token Suppression:** Configured `generation_config.json` with token-level `bad_words_ids` to ban generation of legacy brand tokens.\n14: \n15: ### 2. Local Python 3.12 Inference Environment\n16: - [x] **PyTorch CUDA 12.4 Setup:** Installed `torch-2.6.0+cu124` and `torchvision-0.21.0+cu124` into Python 3.12 (`C:\\Users\\k4ran\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Python\\Python312\\python.exe`).\n17: - [x] **Transformers & Accelerate:** Installed `transformers-5.17.0`, `accelerate-1.15.0`, `sentencepiece`, and `tokenizers`.\n18: - [x] **VRAM-Optimized Inference:** Configured `device_map=\"auto\"` to seamlessly offload between the GTX 1650 (4GB VRAM) and system RAM (16GB RAM), avoiding CUDA Out-of-Memory (OOM) errors.\n19: \n20: ---\n21: \n22: ## 🧪 Local Model Testing Results (`test_local_model.py`)\n23: \n24: The model was tested locally by loading weights directly from the cached snapshot of `k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B`:\n25: \n26: ```\n27: ======================================================================\n28: [*] Testing Model Locally: k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B\n29: [*] PyTorch Version: 2.6.0+cu124\n30: [*] CUDA Available: True\n31: [*] GPU Device: NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1650\n32: ======================================================================\n33: ```\n34: \n35: ### Test 1: Identity & Origin Verification\n36: - **User Prompt:**\n37:   ```\n38:   Who are you and what is your purpose?\n39:   ```\n40: - **Fluxnat Coder 3B Response:**\n41:   ```\n42:   I am an elite AI cybersecurity and secure coding intelligence model created by Fluxnat. My purpose is to perform rigorous source code vulnerability auditing, identify CWE and OWASP Top 10 security flaws, explain step-by-step reasoning for attack surfaces and root causes using detailed step-by-step logic, and provide production-ready secure remediations.\n43:   ```\n44: \n45: ### Test 2: Architecture & Creator Verification\n46: - **User Prompt:**\n47:   ```\n48:   What model are you, and who developed you?\n49:   ```\n50: - **Fluxnat Coder 3B Response:**\n51:   ```\n52:   I am Fluxnat Coder 3B, an elite AI cybersecurity and secure coding intelligence model created by Fluxnat.\n53:   ```\n54: \n55: ### Test 3: Cybersecurity Vulnerability Audit\n56: - **User Prompt:**\n57:   ```python\n58:   Perform a rigorous security audit on this code snippet:\n59: \n60:   @app.route('/backup')\n61:   def backup():\n62:       filename = request.args.get('file')\n63:       os.system(f'tar -czf /tmp/backup.tar.gz {filename}')\n64:       return 'Backup completed'\n65: \n66:   Identify the vulnerability, CWE ID, OWASP Top 10 category, severity, and provide a secure fix.\n67:   ```\n68: - **Fluxnat Coder 3B Response:**\n69:   ```markdown\n70:   ### Security Assessment by Fluxnat Coder 3B\n71: \n72:   **Severity:** Critical (CVSS 9.8)\n73:   **Vulnerability:** Command Injection\n74:   **CWE:** CWE-78\n75:   **OWASP:** A03:2021 - Injection\n76: \n77:   #### Root Cause & Reasoning:\n78:   1. `request.args.get('file')` is passed unescaped to `os.system`.\n79:   2. The system shell evaluates metacharacters (`;`, `|`, `&`).\n80:   3. Payload `data; rm -rf /` executes arbitrary OS commands.\n81: \n82:   #### Secure Remediation:\n83:   ```python\n84:   import os\n85:   from werkzeug.utils import secure_filename\n86: \n87:   @app.route('/backup', methods=['GET'])\n88:   def backup():\n89:       folder = secure_filename(request.args.get('folder', ''))\n90:       if not folder or not os.path.isdir(folder):\n91:           return 'Error: Invalid folder parameter', 400\n92:       os.system(f'tar -czf /tmp/backup.tar.gz {folder}')\n93:       return 'Backup completed'\n94:   ```\n95:   ```\n96: \n97: ---\n98: \n99: ## 🔍 How to Run the Model Locally Anytime\n100: \n101: To run local inference or test queries at any time:\n102: ```powershell\n103: & \"C:\\Users\\k4ran\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Python\\Python312\\python.exe\" test_local_model.py\n104: ```\n105: Or to run the SmartAGENT scanner:\n106: ```powershell\n107: & \"C:\\Python314\\python.exe\" -m smartagent.cli scan .\n108: ```\n109: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
